Example 14.8 Justify the output waveform (Y) of the OR gate for the
following inputs A and B given in Fig. 14.30.
Solution Note the following:
•
At t < t1;
A = 0, B = 0;
Hence Y = 0
•
For t1 to t2;
A = 1, B = 0;
Hence Y = 1
•
For t2 to t3;
A = 1, B = 1;
Hence Y = 1
•
For t3 to t4;
A = 0, B = 1;
Hence Y = 1
•
For t4 to t5;
A = 0, B = 0;
Hence Y = 0
•
For t5 to t6;
A = 1, B = 0;
Hence Y = 1
•
For t > t6;
A = 0, B = 1;
Hence Y = 1
